# Short mW ice/water interface at 270 K.
# The starting frame is input/traj/interface_f0.lammpstrj (timestep 0).
# Real units, Stillinger-Weber mW (Molinero and Moore, J. Phys. Chem. B
# 113, 4008, 2009). The melting point of mW is near 274 K, so 270 K is
# a few kelvin of undercooling. The ensemble is NVT at the snapshot
# volume. One OpenMP thread. Dump every 5000 steps of 10 fs, which is
# 50 ps, including the first step. The run is 1 ns.

units real
atom_style atomic
boundary p p p
atom_modify map array

region box block 0 1 0 1 0 1
create_box 1 box
read_dump interface_f0.lammpstrj 0 x y z box yes add yes

mass 1 18.015
pair_style sw
pair_coeff * * mW.sw mW
neighbor 2.0 bin
neigh_modify every 1 delay 0 check yes

timestep 10.0
thermo 10000
velocity all create 270.0 270 mom yes rot yes dist gaussian
fix 1 all nvt temp 270.0 270.0 100.0
dump 1 all custom 5000 growth.lammpstrj id type x y z
dump_modify 1 sort id first yes
run 100000
